# Subagent Model Restriction

Subagents are fine. Expensive Claude/Opus models are not — they burn Cursor API usage.

## Hard rules

- When using the `Task` tool / spawning subagents, **always** set `model` to one of:
  - `cursor-grok-4.5-high` (Grok) — prefer for exploration, reasoning, general work
  - `composer-2.5-fast` (Composer) — prefer for fast mechanical coding / edits
- **Do not** use Opus, Claude, Sonnet, GPT, or Gemini models for subagents unless the user explicitly names that model.
- If unsure which of the two to pick, default to `cursor-grok-4.5-high`.

## Exception

Only switch to another model when the user explicitly requests it (e.g. "use Opus for this", "spin up a Claude reviewer").
